    "title": "The Best Photos of the Royal Family at the Nigerian State Banquet at Windsor Castle - NewsBreak",
    "text": "8 hours ago For the first time since 1989, the UK is hosting a State Visit from a Nigerian leader. President Bola Tinubu and First Lady Oluremi Tinubu are in the country on a two-day trip, hosted by King Charles and Queen Camilla. This is the also the first time since 1928 that the British royal family has hosted a Muslim head of state during Ramadan, and the first Nigerian leader to be hosted by the British monarch at Windsor Castle. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
